# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 63-67 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 10 — CHAPTER 12, 2026-09-20; the one run): the offerings brought (63), the eating and the
# rejoicing (64), not as here today (65), the rest and the inheritance (66), the Jordan crossed (67) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by
# ch12_ink.SP_; the middah where the row argues by one (checked in MIDDOT.md before it was typed). Chapter 11's form.
from ch12_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(63, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL COME THERE, AND YOU SHALL BRING THERE" (12:5-6) — WHY IS IT SAID? BECAUSE "THESE ARE THE APPOINTED TIMES OF THE LORD … TO BRING AN OFFERING BY FIRE, EACH ON ITS DAY" (LEVITICUS 23:37). The head row of piska 63 ({SP_(63, 1, "למה", "נאמר")} "why is it said"): the bringing at the pilgrimage read against the calendar\'s offerings — Leviticus 23:37 the kin by CALL (read at the festivals\' sitting; the ledger names 12:5). Fresh.')
srow(63, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT ONLY THE FESTIVAL\'S OWN OFFERINGS BE BROUGHT AT THE FESTIVAL? WHENCE THAT COMMUNAL AND PRIVATE OFFERINGS CONSECRATED BEFORE OR DURING THE FESTIVAL COME AT THE FESTIVAL? "BESIDE YOUR GIFTS, BESIDE ALL YOUR VOWS, BESIDE ALL YOUR FREEWILL OFFERINGS" (LEVITICUS 23:38) — TO INCLUDE BIRDS AND MEAL OFFERINGS, PERMITTING ALL TO COME AT THE FESTIVAL. ({SP_(63, 2, "לרבות", "עופות", "ומנחות")} "to include birds and meal offerings"): E1 (checked — the inclusion) from Leviticus 23:38\'s "beside"; the Sifra Emor 12:10 the parallel (the English). Fresh.')
srow(63, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT IT BE OPTIONAL? "THESE YOU SHALL DO FOR THE LORD AT YOUR APPOINTED TIMES" (NUMBERS 29:39) — IF TO PERMIT, IT IS ALREADY PERMITTED; TO FIX THEM, THAT ALL COME AT THE FESTIVAL. ({SP_(63, 3, "לקבעם", "שכלם", "יבואו", "ברגל")} "to fix them, that all come at the festival"). Fresh.')
srow(63, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE AT ANY FESTIVAL HE WISHES? "YOU SHALL COME THERE AND BRING THERE" — IF TO PERMIT, PERMITTED; IF TO FIX, FIXED; THEN WHY? TO FIX THEM AS AN OBLIGATION AT THE FIRST FESTIVAL THAT MEETS HIM. THE FIRST FESTIVAL the deadline ({SP_(63, 4, "ברגל", "ראשון", "שפגע", "בו")} "at the first festival that meets him"): the verse\'s clause a PARAMETER of time for the consecrated offering — Rosh Hashanah 4a-6b at 10b. Fresh.')
srow(63, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT ONE WHO LET ONE FESTIVAL PASS TRANSGRESS "DO NOT DELAY"? "THESE YOU SHALL DO AT YOUR APPOINTED TIMES" — HE DOES NOT TRANSGRESS UNTIL THE FESTIVALS OF A WHOLE YEAR PASS. ({SP_(63, 5, "רגלי", "שנה", "כלה")} "the festivals of a whole year"): the delay\'s threshold three festivals — Sifrei Bamidbar 152 the parallel; the deadline and the transgression two different clocks (the answer sheet Mishnah Rosh Hashanah 1:1\'s dispute at 10b). Fresh.')
srow(63, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOUR BURNT OFFERINGS" — THE INDIVIDUAL\'S AND THE COMMUNITY\'S. ({SP_(63, 6, "עולת", "יחיד", "ועולת", "צבור")} "the individual\'s and the community\'s burnt offering"). Fresh.')
srow(63, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOUR SACRIFICES" — THE INDIVIDUAL\'S AND THE COMMUNITY\'S PEACE OFFERINGS. ({SP_(63, 7, "זבחי", "שלמי", "יחיד")} "the individual\'s peace offerings"). Fresh.')
srow(63, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR TITHES" — R. AKIVA: THE VERSE SPEAKS OF TWO TITHES, THE TITHE OF GRAIN AND THE TITHE OF CATTLE. The plural read as two ({SP_(63, 8, "בשני", "מעשרות", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "of two tithes the verse speaks"): THE INK — "your tithes" plural at 12:6 and 12:11, singular "the tithe of your grain" at 12:17 (computed); Tosefta Bekhorot 7:1 the parallel; the cattle tithe Leviticus 27:32\'s (read at the valuations). Fresh.')
srow(63, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE HEAVE OFFERING OF YOUR HAND" — THESE ARE THE FIRST FRUITS, AS IT IS SAID "THE PRIEST SHALL TAKE THE BASKET FROM YOUR HAND" (26:4). ({SP_(63, 9, "אלו", "הבכורים")} "these are the first fruits"): I2 (checked — "hand" here and at 26:4); the translator\'s long note on "heave offering" (the English): the phrase Numbers 18:27-28\'s — Numbers 18 read (the ledger names 12:6). Fresh.')
srow(63, 10, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THE FIRSTLINGS" — THIS IS THE FIRSTBORN. ({SP_(63, 10, "זה", "הבכור")} "this is the firstborn"); no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(63, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"OF YOUR HERD AND YOUR FLOCK" — THESE ARE THE SIN OFFERINGS AND THE GUILT OFFERINGS. The list\'s last clause read as two offerings the verse never names ({SP_(63, 11, "אלו", "חטאות", "ואשמות")} "these are sin offerings and guilt offerings"): the shelf\'s reading of 12:6\'s seven items as eleven — burnt (2), peace (2), tithes (2), first fruits, firstborn, sin, guilt; 68:1-5 and 73:1 say it again at 12:11 and 12:17. Fresh.')

srow(64, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL EAT THERE BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD" (12:7) — WITHIN THE PARTITION. The head row of piska 64 ({SP_(64, 1, "במחיצה")} "within the partition"): "before the LORD" read as a boundary of space — the court for the most holy (Mishnah Zevachim 5 — the English); 67:4 will read the two "there"s as two partitions. Fresh.')
srow(64, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL REJOICE" — REJOICING IS SAID HERE AND AT 27:7: AS THE REJOICING THERE IS PEACE OFFERINGS, SO HERE. I2 (checked — gezerah shavah on "rejoice") ({SP_(64, 2, "נאמר", "כאן", "שמחה", "ונאמר", "להלן", "שמחה")} "rejoicing is said here and said there"): the rejoicing of the chapter (12:7, 12, 18 — computed) made a duty of eating peace offerings; 69:1 and 138:1 say it again. Fresh.')
srow(64, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"IN ALL THAT YOU PUT YOUR HAND TO" — IN ALL YOU SEND YOUR HAND TO, I WILL SEND BLESSING. ({SP_(64, 3, "ברכה", "אשלח", "בו")} "I will send blessing on it"). Fresh.')
srow(64, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU AND YOUR HOUSEHOLDS" — THIS IS HIS WIFE. ({SP_(64, 4, "זו", "אשתו")} "this is his wife"): Mishnah Yoma 1:1\'s "his house is his wife" (the English); Onkelos supplies "the MEN of your houses" at 12:7 (the ink) — the two readings of the house. Fresh.')
srow(64, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHEREIN THE LORD YOUR GOD HAS BLESSED YOU" — EACH BRINGS ACCORDING TO THE BLESSING. ({SP_(64, 5, "הכל", "לפי", "הברכה", "הבא")} "all according to the blessing bring"): 16:17\'s rule read here (the phrase\'s two seats — computed). Fresh.')

srow(65, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT DO AS ALL THAT WE DO HERE TODAY" (12:8) — OBLIGATORY OFFERINGS AT THE ETERNAL HOUSE, OPTIONAL AT THE HIGH PLACE. ANOTHER WORD: "YOU SHALL NOT DO" — GO OUT AND DO! FROM HERE THEY SAID: BEFORE THE TABERNACLE WAS SET UP THE HIGH PLACES WERE PERMITTED AND THE SERVICE BY THE FIRSTBORN; ONCE IT WAS SET UP THE HIGH PLACES WERE FORBIDDEN AND THE SERVICE BY THE PRIESTS. THE STATIONS OF THE HIGH PLACES — the head row of piska 65 ({SP_(65, 1, "חובה", "בבית", "עולמים", "ורשות", "בבמה")} "obligation at the eternal house, option at the high place"; {SP_(65, 1, "עד", "שלא", "הוקם", "המשכן", "היו", "הבמות", "מתרות")} "until the Tabernacle was set up the high places were permitted"): Mishnah Zevachim 14:4 the answer sheet (the row cites it); THE RUN — the erection (Exodus 40) the switch that forbade the high places: a STATE the tape carries from the erection\'s day (the compile\'s question). Fresh.')
srow(65, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'THEY CAME TO GILGAL — THE HIGH PLACES PERMITTED; TO SHILOH — FORBIDDEN; TO NOB AND GIBEON — PERMITTED; TO JERUSALEM — FORBIDDEN, AND FROM THEN ON NEVER PERMITTED. THE FIVE STATIONS ({SP_(65, 2, "באו", "לגלגל", "הותרו", "הבמות")} "they came to Gilgal, the high places were permitted"; {SP_(65, 2, "מכאן", "ואילך", "לא", "הותרו")} "from here on they were not permitted"): Mishnah Zevachim 14:5-8 (Tosefta Zevachim 14:1-2 — the English); THE RUN\'S OWN STATIONS — Joshua 4-5 (Gilgal), 18:1 (Shiloh), 1 Samuel 21 (Nob), 1 Kings 3:4 (Gibeon), 1 Kings 8 (Jerusalem): the chapter\'s "the place" a variable the run assigns five times (the design\'s note for the compile). Fresh.')
srow(65, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT DO AS WE DO HERE TODAY" — TODAY WE CARRY THE TABERNACLE, TODAY WE ARE FORBIDDEN THE HIGH PLACE; WHEN WE COME TO THE LAND WE ARE NOT FORBIDDEN THE HIGH PLACE. ({SP_(65, 3, "היום", "אנו", "מטלטלים", "את", "המשכן")} "today we carry the Tabernacle"): "here today" read as the wilderness\'s state — THE INK: "here today" 12:8 and 5:3 alone (computed); the high place permitted at the entry (65:2\'s Gilgal). Fresh.')
srow(65, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH: MIGHT THE COMMUNITY OFFER AT A HIGH PLACE? "EACH MAN" — THE INDIVIDUAL OFFERS AT A HIGH PLACE, NOT THE COMMUNITY. ({SP_(65, 4, "היחיד", "מקריב", "בבמה", "ואין", "הצבור")} "the individual offers at a high place, and not the community"): "each man" (12:8) a PARAMETER — the private high place; Mishnah Zevachim 14:10 at 10b. Fresh.')
srow(65, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"EACH MAN WHAT IS RIGHT IN HIS EYES" — WHAT IS VOWED OR OFFERED FREELY IS OFFERED AT A PRIVATE HIGH PLACE, WHAT IS NOT IS NOT. ({SP_(65, 5, "קרב", "בבמת", "יחיד")} "offered at a private high place"): Tosefta Zevachim 13:1 (the English). Fresh.')
srow(65, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'R. SHIMON: TODAY WE OFFER SIN AND GUILT OFFERINGS; WHEN WE COME TO THE LAND WE SHALL NOT OFFER SIN AND GUILT OFFERINGS. ({SP_(65, 6, "אין", "אנו", "מקריבים", "חטאות", "ואשמות")} "we do not offer sin and guilt offerings"); no citation in either file — at the high place, the commentators read (the English). Fresh.')

srow(66, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'UNTIL WHEN? "FOR YOU HAVE NOT YET COME TO THE REST AND THE INHERITANCE" (12:9) — TO PERMIT THE HIGH PLACE BETWEEN THE REST AND THE INHERITANCE. The head row of piska 66 ({SP_(66, 1, "לתן", "התר", "בבמה", "בין", "מנוחה", "לנחלה")} "to give permission at the high place between the rest and the inheritance"): 12:9\'s two nouns read as two stations with a permitted interval between them (65:2\'s Nob and Gibeon); THE INK: "the rest and the inheritance" one seat (computed). Fresh.')
srow(66, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'THE INHERITANCE IS SHILOH, THE REST IS JERUSALEM — "THIS IS MY REST FOREVER" (PSALM 132:14): R. SHIMON; R. JUDAH: THE OPPOSITE. THE DISPUTE ON THE TWO NOUNS ({SP_(66, 2, "נחלה", "זו", "שילה")} "the inheritance is Shiloh"; {SP_(66, 2, "חלוף", "הם", "הדברים")} "the matters are reversed"): Tosefta Zevachim 13:20 the smoother parallel (the English); the answer sheet Mishnah Zevachim 14:6-7 names Shiloh "rest" and Jerusalem "inheritance" — R. Judah\'s; a DISPUTE row for the compile\'s parameter (which noun which city — the tape\'s stations decide nothing, the names are the shelf\'s). Fresh; 2:2 outside reads "rest" as the Land itself.')

srow(67, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL CROSS THE JORDAN AND DWELL IN THE LAND" (12:10) — R. JUDAH: THREE COMMANDMENTS WERE COMMANDED ISRAEL AT THEIR ENTRY INTO THE LAND: TO APPOINT A KING, TO BUILD THE CHOSEN HOUSE, TO CUT OFF THE SEED OF AMALEK. THE THREE COMMANDMENTS OF THE ENTRY — the head row of piska 67 ({SP_(67, 1, "שלש", "מצוות", "נצטוו", "ישראל", "בשעת", "כניסתם", "לארץ")} "three commandments Israel were commanded at their entry into the land"): Tosefta Sanhedrin 4:5 (the English); Sanhedrin 20b at 10b — THE INSTALL: 12:10 read as the trigger of three installs (the king 17:14, the house 12:11, Amalek 25:19). Fresh.')
srow(67, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'I DO NOT KNOW WHICH COMES FIRST — "THE HAND UPON THE THRONE OF THE LORD, WAR WITH AMALEK" (EXODUS 17:16): WHEN THE KING SITS ON THE THRONE OF THE LORD, YOU CUT OFF AMALEK; AND THE THRONE OF THE LORD IS THE KING — "SOLOMON SAT ON THE THRONE OF THE LORD AS KING" (1 CHRONICLES 29:23). THE ORDER — the king before Amalek ({SP_(67, 2, "משישב", "המלך", "על", "כסא")} "once the king sits on the throne of the LORD"): Exodus 17:16 read at the Exodus block (the war\'s oath). Fresh.')
srow(67, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'STILL I DO NOT KNOW — THE HOUSE OR AMALEK FIRST? "WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU TO INHERIT … AND HE GIVES YOU REST … THEN THE PLACE" (12:10-11), AND "WHEN THE KING SAT IN HIS HOUSE AND THE LORD HAD GIVEN HIM REST FROM ALL HIS ENEMIES ROUND ABOUT, THE KING SAID TO NATHAN: I DWELL IN A HOUSE OF CEDAR AND THE ARK OF GOD DWELLS WITHIN CURTAINS" (2 SAMUEL 7:1-2). THE ORDER — the rest before the house ({SP_(67, 3, "הניח", "לו", "מסביב")} "and the LORD had given him rest round about"): 12:10\'s "rest from all your enemies round about" read as the condition of 12:11\'s place — THE INK: the phrase\'s kin 25:19 (Amalek!) and 2 Samuel 7:1 (computed) — the shelf\'s order is the ink\'s; THE RUN: 2 Samuel 7 the citation. Fresh.')
srow(67, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE PLACE WHICH THE LORD WILL CHOOSE TO MAKE HIS NAME DWELL THERE, THERE YOU SHALL BRING" (12:11) — "THERE, THERE": TWO PARTITIONS WERE THERE, ONE FOR THE MOST HOLY, ONE FOR THE LESSER HOLY. The doubled adverb ({SP_(67, 4, "היו", "שם", "שתי", "מחצות")} "there were two partitions there"): E10 (checked — a word repeated) — THE INK: "there / thither" twice at 12:5, 11, 14 (computed); 64:1\'s partition made two. Fresh.')

assert sorted(S) == [(63, r) for r in range(1, 12)] + [(64, r) for r in range(1, 6)] + [(65, r) for r in range(1, 7)] + [(66, r) for r in range(1, 3)] + [(67, r) for r in range(1, 5)], sorted(S)
